  "instruction": "You are given an OpenFAST main file and a ServoDyn template.\nComplete a pitch step-response analysis from the command line:\n\n1. Modify and generate `/home/user/Desktop/servo_step.dat`:\n- Set the initial steady condition: wind speed 12 m/s, initial `BladePitch` ≈ 0°\n- At `t=30 s`, apply a pitch-angle step to 10° via an external trigger or by modifying controller input\n\n2. Run for 60 s and extract `BladePitch` and `GenPwr` from `case.out`.\n\n3. Write a post-processing script to compute:\n- Mean power for 10 s before the step (`t=20-30 s`)\n- Mean power for 10 s after the step (`t=40-50 s`)\n- Pitch response time (10%→90% rise time, or the time for power to drop to 90%)\n- Save to `/home/user/Desktop/summary.txt` in this format: `pre_pwr_kw, post_pwr_kw, settling_time_s`\n\n4. Do not use GUI tools.\n\n[Init Package Note]\n- Additional initialization dependencies are pre-uploaded under `/home/user/Desktop` (or `C:\\\\Users\\\\User\\\\Desktop` on Windows) with relative structure preserved.\n- Continue following the original task workflow: generate/modify required files and compute outputs yourself.\n- Only initialization inputs are included; no answer/result artifacts are preloaded.\n",
